<title>USA: TACA calls for open skies with US, Central America.</title>
<headline>TACA calls for open skies with US, Central America.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federico Bloch, president of TACA International Airlines, defended his controversial alliance with American Airlines and called for open skies between the United States and all of Central America.</p>
<p>&quot;If we are not part of an alliance, we are going to get tromped over,&quot; he told the Americas Conference on Aviation on Thursday.</p>
<p>With fare cutting and attractive frequent flier programs, the big U.S. carriers are grabbing ever larger shares of the Latin American market.</p>
</text>
